## Governance Model: Voluntary Delegation
Voluntary delegation blends direct and representative democracy, allowing individuals to vote directly or delegate to trusted proxies. Inspired by philosophical debates, it ensures broad participation and efficiency.

### Historical Context
- **Jean-Jacques Rousseau**: Advocated for direct democracy, emphasizing the people’s will as the source of legitimacy.
- **James Madison**: Proposed representation to moderate factions, ensuring stability and expertise in governance.

### Implementation
- **Online Platforms**: Digital committees enable real-time voting and policy discussions, accessible globally.
- **NGOs**: Represent opposition and marginalized voices, ensuring a balanced democratic infrastructure.
- **Voluntary Delegation Paper**: Outlines the model’s mechanics, visualized below (attachment id:0).

**Visualization**: Delegation Flow
```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Voter] -->|Delegates to| B[Proxy]
    B -->|Delegates to| C[Another Proxy]
    C -->|Votes on| D[Proposal]
    A -->|Direct Vote| D
    D -->|Feedback Loop| E[Community Review]